00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
rainbow six extraction takes the  framework of rainbow six siege a pvp  game and reimagines it in a pve setting  with three people working as a team to  defeat the alien threat known as the  arkians while a lot of your rainbow six  siege skills will transfer over it is  also quite different in a number of key  ways which is why after playing the game  for over 20 hours we have 15 tips to  help you out when you first start  rainbow six extraction and if you find  these tips useful why not hit the like  and sub button it really helps us out a  lot okay so probably the most important  thing when it comes to rainbow six  whether it's siege or extraction is your  teamwork i don't know about you but i  never like playing rainbow six siege  with randos i always play with a  personal party of close friends that i  know and that goes doubly so for  extraction with siege at least you can  just rely on your brandos being good at  shooting people but with extraction you  have to constantly be communicating due  to the objective based nature of the  game like yeah you can solo but i  wouldn't recommend it okay but say you  do want to play some and your friends  aren't available so i'm gonna hop into  the solo queue you're gonna need to talk  with a headset the pings are okay but  they're not gonna cut it so either get  used to talking on the mic with randos  or only play with your friends and  that's because communication starts  right away on the operator select screen  so every round of extraction is called  an incursion and every incursion is  broken up into three sub zones each with  randomly generated objectives  at the start of an incursion you can see  each objective very clearly and certain  operators are better for certain  objectives for example if you want to  locate tech objects you want to pick iq  or if you need to sneak up and stealth  kill particular archians this can be  done with stealth characters like vigil  the key is to spend a moment and talk  with your team look at your objectives  see what you need and make sure all the  roles are being properly filled a big  part of this game is leveling up your  overall career it's how you unlock new  operators new maps and new equipment  playing on higher difficulties does  improve the rewards and the xp you gain  but the best way to boost up your levels  are the games studies which are  extractions versions of map specific  in-game challenges each map has several  pages of challenges and each page  features three studies you'll need to  complete the current page you're on  before you can unlock the next page of  objectives and there's no way to change  them so you're kind of just stuck with  whatever objective you currently have if  you want to be leveling up at a  consistent pace it's important to be  focusing on these studies now the  problem with this is that studies can  require you to do things that may be  misaligned with your current objective  the reality is sometimes you might just  have to go rogue and do your own thing  and only care about yourself but if  you're playing with friends the best  thing to do is just communicate with  each other and decide hey we're going  specifically into this incursion just to  focus on these studies and then get back  out we did this plenty of times  throughout our play and we found we were  able to level up pretty consistently  speaking of studies sometimes they will  call for killing very particular types  of argens this can be a little bit  frustrating because what archaeans spawn  on the map is randomized so there's no  way to go into a map guaranteeing that  you will find that particular arcane  that you need for the study however you  can improve your chances by playing on  harder difficulties for example there  are some enemy types that just straight  up will not spawn on the base moderate  difficulty so if you're trying to find  say tormentors on alaska don't play on  moderate difficulty play on at least  cautious to guarantee that some  tormentors might show up and from there  with each difficulty it just increases  the chances of these more rare types of  archaeans showing up another key to a  successful extraction is good nest  management nests are the glowing spores  from which virtually all of these  sub-zones archaeans spawn from and each  subzone begins with these nest line  dormant the trick specifically on higher  difficulties is to employ stealth by  taking out nests quietly you'll avoid  stirring them into spawning many more  archaeans once an archaean spots you  it'll perform a shrieking scream that  will alert nearby nests permanently  activating them with a more steady  stream of archaeans spawning out it's  rarely a good idea to go into an  incursion guns blazing you want to start  stealthing as much as possible this  means there's pretty much no reason not  to have a silencer attached of course  you should always be performing stealthy  melee takedowns to save on ammo  especially on harder difficulties where  ammo is at a premium take the time to  look at the attachments on your  operator's weapons and put on silencers  whenever possible of course this is  rainbow six so there might be times when  you need to use a big hulk and shotgun  to blast a hole through a wall we found  this tactic to be not quite as necessary  as it is in siege however there are  times where we found ourselves doing  this either to avoid a certain group of  enemies get to an objective faster or  make a quick escape something cool to  note is that in extraction you have a  special flashlight affixed to the front  of your gun at all times that can  actually let you see aliens through  breakable walls this is a great way to  be able to identify archians easily and  shoot them through the walls without  ever putting yourself in danger  a certain video game muscle memory that  you're gonna have to abandon when  playing extraction is the idea that you  need to always push through no matter  what an extraction is often better to  extract early and save yourself a lot of  headache  sometimes a run just goes wrong allies  die you lose a significant chunk of your  health and realistically you don't think  you're gonna make it to the end if  that's the way you're feeling cut out  early if you end up dying you will lose  that operator as well as a good chunk of  your progression xp and you won't get it  back until you go rescue them also you  get a pretty large xp bonus if you  extract with your full squad so going  the rest of the way solo might not net  you as much xp as it would extracting  with your full party another important  thing is to manage your resource  supplies resources come in the forms of  react gear abilities ammo and health and  all of them are very important to keep  full up when you bring up the map menu  you actually have a live tracker of how  many resource caches are left in the  active subzone you're in always double  check this if you're looking for  something like a health kit so you're  not wasting time looking for something  that might not even be there and of  course because these are limited you do  want to make sure you're sharing them  with your teammate the reality is  especially on earlier difficulties you  don't need all that ammo but your ally  might so it's always good to just  communicate with everybody and make sure  everyone is topped up and has everything  they need if finding resource caches is  a big priority for your team make sure  to have someone play as iq whose ability  lets you easily find them you can also  point out resource caches using the ping  system i said before that the ping  system isn't a replacement for mics and  that is true but you should still be  just pinging everything all the time  ping enemies ping spores ping resource  caches ping ping ping okay here's like a  really quick tip that's just kind of  nice to know whenever you're moving  along to the next sub zone you need to  have two players activate it in order  for it to start counting down however  that countdown is 30 seconds if you just  want to speed things up have the third  player come in and also activate it and  it will switch to a 5 second countdown  this can be incredibly useful if the  extraction zone is hot and you're trying  to get out of there asap or you're just  looking to speed things along if you  want to make an objective easier in this  game the key is to spend as much time  scouting the surrounding area of the  objective as possible that means killing  arcanes and destroying nests there are  certain objectives that will alert  nearby nests and they will start  spawning archians in so if you destroy  them beforehand it'll make things a lot  easier for you  if you're ever trying to do a mission  where you're rescuing an operator a way  to make it really easy is just to go  around the area of the archaean tree and  destroy all the little nests when you  actually activate the rescue attempt it  doesn't spawn more arcane so as long as  you destroyed all the nests you should  be able to save them without any extra  stress something you'll have to worry  about throughout this game is sprawl  which is the  gross goo that just covers the entire  map archaeans spawn it nest spawn it it  can be a real pain because you move  slower and sprawl and archaeans move  faster and can sometimes do more damage  in sprawl it gets even worse on harder  difficulties where you can get a  mutation where sprawl turns green and  becomes poisonous so how do you manage  sprawl first off always kill enemies in  their weak points when you kill an enemy  normally they actually leave sprawl  behind when they die but if you kill  them in their weak point they do not  leave down sprawl arcane weak points are  pretty obvious it's the pink glowish hue  that you can see on their body so just  aim for that and you should be fine of  course what do you do when you already  have sprawl to deal with there is a cool  laser tool you can get that can remove  sprawl for you but you don't get that  until level 25 which is a long ways out  instead you just want to shoot it or  melee it although melee is very very  slow so probably just shoot it having  full mobility is a huge plus so it's  really important that you take the time  to shoot all the sprawl before you start  an objective or to help create a path  for a planned route that you need to  take and really that kind of sums up the  whole ethos around this game it's about  scouting things out in advance planning  your routes planning your objectives and  then acting accordingly if you play  smart and communicate with your team you  will be knocking out incursions like  nobody's business and having a pretty  fun time doing it but of course there's  probably some tips we missed so if you  have any advice to give to your fellow  rainbow six players throw them down in  the comments below and thanks for  watching

